<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins new German paging order.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins new German paging order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Monday it had been awarded a contract to extend the paging network of German paging operator MINIRUF.</p>
<p>Ericsson said it had been the main supplier to MINIRUF since the German operator got a licence in 1994 to run a paging network.</p>
<p>Its paging service, known under the name Quix, now reaches 80 percent of the German population with every third pager sold in Germany a Quix pager.</p>
<p>No financial details of the contract were released.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
